# Feature Discovery

Canonical source: `/Users/macbook/Github/vibeCodingRules/feature-discovery.md`

## When to Grill

MUST grill (3–5 questions) when the task **changes behavior** users or clients will observe — small UX, validation, API shape, or permission changes included.

### Skip triggers (any one true)

- User explicitly waives discovery ("just implement", "no questions").
- Clear bugfix with reproduction steps — no design choice.
- Mechanical work only: dep bump, formatter/linter, copying rules, config sync.
- Typo, copy, or formatting-only — no behavior change.
- Rename or move with zero behavior change.

If none apply → grill.

## How to Grill

- Ask 3–5 focused questions in one message; prefer structured choice UI when options are finite.
- Cover: goal, acceptance criteria, out of scope, data/permissions, UX/error cases, preferred approach if options exist.
- If the user says "just do it" or answers, stop grilling and implement.
- If still unclear after answers, ask one more tight question — do not loop.

## User signal

If the user says "grill me", treat as ambiguous and run discovery even if the task looked specified.

## Rule disagreements

If a MUST rule seems wrong for the task: grill and propose a rulebook change. Agents MUST NOT silently override rules.
